                <pb facs="0569" n="463" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg463"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Sleeper to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-08-30"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 30,
                    1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Sleeper quotes a telegram received from the Santiago consulate, which says
                    that there is reliable private information that General Rabi and other prominent
                    generals of the liberating army left that morning for Habana at the request of
                    the Government for the purpose of conferring with insurgent leaders with a view
                    to effecting a compromise of existing troubles. He also says that the legation
                    has been privately informed that these generals were requested by the Government
                    to take the field against the revolutionists, and that they offered in lieu
                    thereof to appoint a committee to endeavor to effect amicable settlement.)</p>
            </div>
